---
title: Multiple forms
description: Render several independent `superForm` instances on one page by giving each its own ID.
---

<script>
	import { Callout } from "$lib/markdown";
</script>

One page, two forms, same schema — each must track its own values, errors and submission state. The rule is simple: every `superForm` call gets its own `id`, and each `Field` is passed the form instance it belongs to.

## Two instances from one validated form

The server validates once; the component creates two independent `superForm` instances from the same data:

```ts title="src/routes/accounts/+page.server.ts"
import { superValidate } from "sveltekit-superforms";
import { zod } from "sveltekit-superforms/adapters";
import { profileSchema } from "./schema.js";

export const load = async () => ({
	form: await superValidate(zod(profileSchema)),
});
```

```svelte title="src/routes/accounts/profile-forms.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { untrack } from "svelte";
	import { superForm, type SuperValidated } from "sveltekit-superforms";
	import { Control, Field, Label } from "@emmorts/formsnap";
	import type { ProfileData } from "./schema.js";

	let { validated }: { validated: SuperValidated<ProfileData> } = $props();

	const primaryForm = superForm(untrack(() => validated), {
		id: "profile-primary",
		resetForm: false,
	});
	const secondaryForm = superForm(untrack(() => validated), { id: "profile-secondary" });

	const { form: primaryData, enhance: enhancePrimary } = primaryForm;
	const { form: secondaryData, enhance: enhanceSecondary } = secondaryForm;
</script>

<form method="POST" use:enhancePrimary>
	<Field form={primaryForm} name="email" fieldErrors>
		<Control>
			{#snippet children({ props })}
				<Label>Primary email</Label>
				<input {...props} bind:value={$primaryData.email} />
			{/snippet}
		</Control>
		{#snippet description()}Used for account recovery.{/snippet}
	</Field>
	<button type="submit">Save primary</button>
</form>

<form method="POST" use:enhanceSecondary>
	<Field form={secondaryForm} name="email" fieldErrors>
		<Control>
			{#snippet children({ props })}
				<Label>Secondary email</Label>
				<input {...props} bind:value={$secondaryData.email} />
			{/snippet}
		</Control>
		{#snippet description()}Used for notifications.{/snippet}
	</Field>
	<button type="submit">Save secondary</button>
</form>
```

## Separate actions per form

When each form posts to its own named action, validate with the matching `id` on the server too, so Superforms routes the result back to the right instance:

```ts title="src/routes/accounts/+page.server.ts"
import { fail } from "@sveltejs/kit";
import { superValidate } from "sveltekit-superforms";
import { zod } from "sveltekit-superforms/adapters";
import { profileSchema } from "./schema.js";

export const load = async () => ({
	primary: await superValidate(zod(profileSchema), { id: "profile-primary" }),
	secondary: await superValidate(zod(profileSchema), { id: "profile-secondary" }),
});

async function save(request: Request, id: string) {
	const form = await superValidate(request, zod(profileSchema), { id });
	if (!form.valid) return fail(400, { form });
	return { form };
}

export const actions = {
	primary: ({ request }) => save(request, "profile-primary"),
	secondary: ({ request }) => save(request, "profile-secondary"),
};
```

Each form then posts with `action="?/primary"` or `action="?/secondary"`.

## How it works

- The `id` option is what keeps instances apart. Without one, Superforms warns about duplicate form IDs and the forms begin to share page state.
- Field IDs belong to the component instance, so two forms never generate the same target — labels and descriptions never cross over.
- Each instance keeps its own `form`, `errors`, `message` and `submitting` stores; clearing one form's errors leaves the other untouched.

<Callout type="warning">

A successful submission re-runs the route's `load`, and every form whose ID appears in the refreshed data rebinds to it — dropping that form's unsaved values and errors. Return the saved record from `load` to keep it, or set Superforms' `invalidateAll: false` on a form that must not refresh page data.

</Callout>
